{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning",
    "title": "Treatment Planning",
    "order": 13
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning-head-and-neck",
    "title": "Head & Neck Treatment Planning",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "The Vertebral Body Is Your Roadmap",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In head and neck radiation therapy, the cervical vertebral bodies are your most reliable landmark \u2014 field borders and contouring decisions are constantly described in relation to the C-spine. This lesson connects the key anatomical structures you need to treat (or spare) to their corresponding vertebral level, exactly the skill you'll need reading any H&N planning CT."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "C1\u2013C2 \u2014 The Nasopharynx and Oropharynx",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Level"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Structure / Event"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "C1",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Nasopharynx (the uppermost pharynx). The Node of Rouvi\u00e8re, a key retropharyngeal lymph node, sits anterior to C1\u2013C2."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "C2",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Oropharynx begins here, extending down to C3."
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "C3 \u2014 Where Three Structures Begin",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "C3",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " is a genuinely important landmark: the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "epiglottis",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " sits here, marking the superior border of both the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "larynx",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " and the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "hypopharynx",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " \u2014 both structures begin at this level."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which vertebral level marks the epiglottis and the start of both the larynx and hypopharynx?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "C1",
              "C3"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "C3 is where the epiglottis sits, marking the superior border of both the larynx and hypopharynx."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "C4\u2013C5 \u2014 The Glottis",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "true vocal cords (glottis)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 the main functional body of the larynx \u2014 sit at roughly "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "C4\u2013C5",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "pyriform sinuses",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " of the hypopharynx lie lateral to the larynx at this same level, continuing posteriorly alongside it."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "C6 \u2014 Where Three Structures End (or Begin)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "At "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "C6",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ": the larynx ends at the inferior border of the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "cricoid cartilage",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "; the hypopharynx also ends here, emptying into the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "esophagus",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ", which begins just after the cricoid cartilage at this same level."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "At C6, which cartilage marks the end of the larynx?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Thyroid cartilage",
              "Cricoid cartilage"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The cricoid cartilage's inferior border marks the end of the larynx at C6, right where the esophagus begins."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
